# How Lifecycle Rules Work
A rule can apply to all objects in a bucket or only those with a prefix (like logs/) or tags (like project=archive).

Lifecycle actions include:

Transition actions – Move objects between storage classes:

Example: After 30 days → move from S3 Standard to S3 Standard-IA.

Example: After 365 days → move to S3 Glacier Deep Archive.

Expiration actions – Permanently delete objects:

Example: Delete objects after 730 days.

Example: Delete incomplete multipart uploads after 7 days.


#

{
  "Rules": [
    {
      "ID": "Move-Logs-To-Glacier-And-Delete",
      "Filter": {
        "Prefix": "logs/"
      },
      "Status": "Enabled",
      "Transitions": [
        {
          "Days": 30,
          "StorageClass": "STANDARD_IA"
        },
        {
          "Days": 90,
          "StorageClass": "GLACIER"
        }
      ],
      "Expiration": {
        "Days": 365
      },
      "NoncurrentVersionExpiration": {
        "NoncurrentDays": 30
      }
    }
  ]
}
